    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Corbin Carroll**, whose 87.14 score stands as our elite anchor. Facing Mike Paredes, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a sub-5.00 xERA starter, with his dynamic platoon advantage and top-tier order placement cementing him as the must-start of the day. Supporting him, **Gabriel Moreno** (69.89) and **Brice Turang** (68.09) offer high-floor efficiency. **Brice Turang** is particularly intriguing; while his base projection is solid, the matchup against Bryce Elder\u2014a pitcher with a slow delivery\u2014creates a favorable environment for **Brice Turang** to hunt stolen bases, a critical scarcity we are aggressively targeting today. **James Wood** also remains a cornerstone of the outfield, maintaining a strong 67.46 despite facing Nick Martinez, largely because his elite xwOBA (0.404) provides a buffer even against tougher SP profiles.\n\nThe rotation was settled after a tight deliberation at the bench spots, where **Max Muncy** (45.18) was the most difficult exclusion. While **Max Muncy** benefited from a positive park factor against Reid Detmers, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to **Henry Bolte** (44.66) to balance platoon distribution, as **Max Muncy**\u2019s lower order placement (#8) ultimately suppressed his efficiency score below the utility threshold. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players, notably **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, as any shift from their projected #9 spots could cause a significant downward drift in their respective scores. While **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Seiya Suzuki** both carry risk due to facing high-tier arms in Reid Detmers and Dylan Cease, their specific park advantages provide just enough mathematical cushion to justify their presence in the starting lineup over bench options like **Cole Young** or **Zach McKinstry**.",
